jobs.objective:
Version 4 of the ETH indicator lab: a PRECISION TOP/BOTTOM PICKER for ETH on 1m, 3m, 5m and 15m. Continue this project and keep the v1-v3 code, data and widget. Drop all trading requirements: no fees, no PnL, no leverage, no trade rules. The only goal is to call local tops and bottoms as precisely and as early as possible, using closed bars only, and to measure that precision with hard numbers.

TARGET (hindsight labels, used only for scoring): swing pivots from a ZigZag per TF at several scales, (a) k x ATR14 with k = 2, 3, 5 and (b) fixed 0.3%, 0.6%, 1.2% (1m/3m) or 0.6%, 1.2%, 2.5% (5m/15m). The scorer must also accept any other sensible pivot definition you add.

PREDICTION: at each closed bar the model may output nothing, or a TOP or BOTTOM call with a probability 0-1 and an optional price zone. The call must use information up to that bar's close only. The signal may confirm a pivot after it happens (for example 1-3 bars later); measure that lag honestly.

METRICS (per TF, per pivot scale, per probability threshold):
- precision (a call counts if a true pivot of that type lies within +-W bars, W = 3 by default, also report W = 1, 5);
- recall of true pivots;
- the median and p90 of |price error| between the call bar's close and the true extreme, in bp and in ATR;
- the timing lag in bars (signed);
- false calls per day;
- calibration (reliability curve, Brier score, log loss);
- PR-AUC, and lift over the base rate and over simple baselines (layered-BB pivots, the RSI state top/bottom, both-sigma-beyond-2, the first outer-band breach, all from v1/v2).
Report precision@recall curves and pick operating points (high-precision, balanced). Always report the best model per TF even if it is weak.

DATA (use anything public with real history for ETH and state coverage): OKX and Binance USD-M klines (taker-buy volume), Binance aggTrades and bookDepth / bookTicker archives on data.binance.vision (CVD, trade-size imbalance, depth imbalance, spread), funding history (OKX, Binance), open interest (Binance openInterestHist and archive metrics, and what OKX rubik provides), the long/short ratios Binance exposes, Hyperliquid public candles/funding, Deribit public option data if usable (IV, skew, put/call), BTC and ETH/BTC context, and time of day / session. Liquidation feeds without real history may be used only for a live-only feature: flag it and exclude it from scored claims.

MODELS: anything that works. That covers rules, confluence scores, gradient-boosted trees, logistic/ordinal models, sequence models if they validate, multi-timeframe stacks (higher-TF state gating lower-TF calls), and meta-labelling of base signals. Explore widely and push hard: thousands of configs and feature sets are fine.

ANTI-OVERFIT (non-negotiable): time-ordered nested CV with purging and embargo; all v1-v3 holdouts and v3's 2024 final are burned (development only, say so). Before any search, fetch and SEAL a new untouched final period: a full ETH year never used in v1-v3 (for example 2025, verified against the data manifests), plus every ETH bar newer than the v3 cache, and BTC on that same sealed year. Freeze the finalists, then open the seal once. Count every config in the multiple-testing correction (permutation test of PR-AUC or precision vs shuffled-label nulls, block-preserving).

